OL,3,AIf hackers can take control of a
OL,4,Asupermarket freezer, how vulnerable is
OL,5,Aother tech?
OL,6,
OL,7,FSupermarkets across Europe have been
OL,8,Fhit by a suspected cyber-attack
OL,9,Faffecting their fridges and freezers,
OL,10,Fand raising concern about the
OL,11,Fvulnerabilities of internet-connected
OL,12,Fhardware from industrial machinery to
OL,13,Fhumble domestic appliances.
OL,15,FSmart devices which are connected to
OL,16,Fthe internet can include fridges,
OL,17,Fcentral heating, and even washing
OL,18,Fmachines.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1793684893
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AIf hackers can take control of a
OL,4,Asupermarket freezer, how vulnerable is
OL,5,Aother tech?
OL,6,
OL,7,FAnd while that makes them easier to
OL,8,Fcontrol remotely, in theory, any device
OL,9,Fwhich goes online can potentially be
OL,10,Fexploited by malicious actors.
OL,12,FHowever, that doesn't mean hackers can
OL,13,Feasily take control of it, and big
OL,14,Fbrands generally go to great lengths to
OL,15,Fmake sure their tech is secure.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
